[{"id":"VRCE-2-99-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":99,"verse":1,"english":"As Bharata was again ng in this strain, his graceful elder brother, having been highly honoured, answered Bharata in the midst of his relatives, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.507,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-107-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2099001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e15828ea172eeb3f7cb7619c28d06892d2d012a6e3ede2cd48c60ecd9bfd17c3","compact":"c409f7c876e1505885576562e834f48b1fc8a4bd9e97a43b7e80c340f2c8b9dd","nasal":"10b0a180e08f8cd891862cd312c8e163f0dbbf4fcfd21256f225209696036199"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-99-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":99,"verse":2,"english":"Having been born as a son to Daśaratha, foremost of monarchs, by Kaikeyſ, this speech of yours is worthy of you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-107-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2099002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2d76eb77b4fd5bcaac9ab68d522a7beb5861c1a598ecaa6819aaf29d8318e092","compact":"cc1d926e246ad257a32e7b6dd35e875300d0994ed8600b0c4beb3b4b821301ee","nasal":"e3f19f6b0860f6895c1957d93131ceba369398ae870678fddbb48f9b437428c6"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-99-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":99,"verse":3,"english":"O brother, formerly when our father espoused the hand of your mother, he promised her the kingdom as her marriage portion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-107-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2099003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"29b6a47e610d43af532a19d9839824fa7b6e9de3a7a7e7209bc40ec4eafd370d","compact":"841f312d51ed296471540f4fd5b5703753b3aa02a3d6461098098086882623f4","nasal":"841f312d51ed296471540f4fd5b5703753b3aa02a3d6461098098086882623f4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-99-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":99,"verse":4,"english":"Then on the occasion of the war between the gods and the Asuras, that master, the king, well pleased (with her), being besought, granted her a boon.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-107-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2099004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ce1aee7458b94d0408725237ffa6071bc33b5e5e55f5757844d189fde29d39c4","compact":"52b6d82152f8463153bbff40431fc74ecb43882ba1a38763aa6777e3b6a73f6f","nasal":"52b6d82152f8463153bbff40431fc74ecb43882ba1a38763aa6777e3b6a73f6f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-99-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":99,"verse":5,"english":"Having been thus promised, that virtuous lady, your illustrious mother, O foremost of men, asked for two boons (of the king), viz., your enthronement, O best of men, and my banishment. Thus besought by her, the king conferred on her the boon.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-107-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2099005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b3ec822d01bd5ea35fae1cbfa9d123c91e2d65d38b1b3f8a55a7177c7c46f066","compact":"950dee84b4caffd8b192df8e8a0c9a4c592ac03a6cf2aaeece4664438a455fba","nasal":"950dee84b4caffd8b192df8e8a0c9a4c592ac03a6cf2aaeece4664438a455fba"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-99-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":99,"verse":6,"english":"Having been thus promised, that virtuous lady, your illustrious mother, O foremost of men, asked for two boons (of the king), viz., your enthronement, O best of men, and my banishment. Thus besought by her, the king conferred on her the boon.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-107-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2099006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ec25f6bd7b3020ab2b97554bcbb25ab14b823cfd02f9656d6f7bae651027103c","compact":"e19ced8fe8a37dcf0e9f49e11ada56cff52f5256d7ba15ddcc0917396cdb67e5","nasal":"e19ced8fe8a37dcf0e9f49e11ada56cff52f5256d7ba15ddcc0917396cdb67e5"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-99-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":99,"verse":7,"english":"And, you foremost of men, I have been enjoyed by my sire to stay in the woods for fourteen years, in consequence of his having granted her the boon.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-107-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2099007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1c1ad5c453a83c80439337d914902a3dc4bfb610c4b6534ea6e879a7970747b7","compact":"f8bc1090d73c550affb524c582085ebbb5f4203d1cf91431063c999c13e0c785","nasal":"f8bc1090d73c550affb524c582085ebbb5f4203d1cf91431063c999c13e0c785"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-99-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":99,"verse":8,"english":"And, having, in company with Laksmana and Sītā, come to the lone forest, I in humble guise am staying in the truthful speech of my father.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.847,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-107-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2099008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eeaeba443ef23b0890adca640818c8c566b7b11168efc3fa7489f39b756d8241","compact":"8bc58c6a882338c873540a5700b1e0d8f110dd4d372aa5b49c8a7fb1e779de23","nasal":"a921a151648dc52da41df8eda32cd367092644229c987641cad0c720c2c4e235"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-99-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":99,"verse":9,"english":"You too, you foremost of kings, should in the same way speedily render our father truthful, by getting yourself installed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.656,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-107-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2099009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1e9cfe73cda42a1974d3bb864a5771546365ec5003c4d1e345ba8f2ff8ffde85","compact":"b2ec376ad67f3d6bbe422802981c6f277c4f50ecb068716ac524b16632acb0bd","nasal":"f808e96f0578d1606429266f1867aa4ac464419336202205b01fa329be3c9ba0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-99-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":99,"verse":10,"english":"O Bharata, for my sake, do you free that lord, the king, from his debts. Do you, O you cognizant of morality, deliver our father and gladden your mother.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-107-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2099010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f95efdd19d0dd3c3bc3e009599b0c055b7dbc81a5aad718de6cc73386a442c6d","compact":"d1cbcedf127b56d8176378169b59cca122f5e3fc34de12e4b5f20ed3f806d1c5","nasal":"6c666496d0298c0ef4ee9d32c2b632e19c1e54918bb881a5f91d61561fcabb83"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-99-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":99,"verse":11,"english":"O child, we hear that in Gaya, formerly the famous Gaya, engaged in a sacrifice, chanted this Vedic hymn, for pleasing his departed ancestors.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.525,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-107-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2099011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"97533f500aefd92c64dc88e8880c254e0936046eb2edf56b339d1a6ee5e8f152","compact":"97383b11dfbcb2b6fba201fb8a7ba9e958e6f6259338082c1e90dded86c6b93b","nasal":"97383b11dfbcb2b6fba201fb8a7ba9e958e6f6259338082c1e90dded86c6b93b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-99-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":99,"verse":12,"english":"Since a son delivers his sire form the hell named Put, a son goes by the appellation of putra, he protecting his (departed) ancestors in every way.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.658,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-107-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2099012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"85dabb358786c675b0ef0184b1f200625b414698a15640f31898a280314d709b","compact":"e894c446b02b773acc528c0f26786b39557378bf7014b5b5faaccf51af049965","nasal":"e894c446b02b773acc528c0f26786b39557378bf7014b5b5faaccf51af049965"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-99-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":99,"verse":13,"english":"One should wish for many sons crowned with qualities and versed in various lore, for the chance is that one at least of these may repair to Gayā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-107-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2099013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2da95f6c0e2e852b49186182006b74708cceb1e9aadf53aa91c1de63e3dbd122","compact":"8d60273f15c5b30ba41a55513e784c68755a9bf45ec41798da30a8960f1c2d6e","nasal":"22d2ad2ecb30566929f1ad516abb571380e6dd77e413f428f47f5ea26e9fa842"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-99-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":99,"verse":14,"english":"O son of the Raghu race, the Rājarşis have delivered their decision on the point. Therefore, you foremost of men, do you, O lord, rescue your sire from hell.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-107-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2099014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"00b5d34ae44b4d086dab4dc7dbcd50a852a93f81b